 {"id":"r8-011","answer":["lived"],"other_correct":[["could live"]],"wrong_options_that_fit":"","instruction_problem":"The gap takes 'missing word(s)', so 'could live' (fully correct and natural: she can't live nearer, e.g. because of work) must be accepted or the cue should force one word.","level_problem":"","sense_problem":""},
 {"id":"r8-012","answer":["could"],"other_correct":[["was able to"],["were able to"]],"wrong_options_that_fit":"","instruction_problem":"No bracketed cue (unlike the other typed gaps); 'was/were able to' is also correct in a 'word(s)' gap.","level_problem":"","sense_problem":""},
 {"id":"r8-013","answer":"I wish I spoke French.","other_correct":["I wish I could speak French.","I wish I knew French."],"wrong_options_that_fit":"","instruction_problem":"'I wish I could speak French' is at least as natural as 'spoke' and must be accepted.","level_problem":"","sense_problem":""},
 {"id":"r8-014","answer":"If only I had enough time.","other_correct":["If only I had enough time!","If only I had more time.","If only I had more time!"],"wrong_options_that_fit":"","instruction_problem":"Learners will naturally end 'If only...' with '!'; make sure the checker accepts it. 'more time' is an equally natural rewrite.","level_problem":"","sense_problem":""},
 {"id":"r8-015","answer":"I wish my job wasn't boring.","other_correct":["I wish my job weren't boring.","I wish my job was not boring.","I wish my job were not boring.","I wish my job was more interesting.","I wish my job were more interesting.","I wish my job was less boring.","I wish my job were less boring.","I wish my job wasn't so boring.","I wish I had a more interesting job."],"wrong_options_that_fit":"","instruction_problem":"Very open: many correct rewrites (wasn't/weren't/was not, more interesting, less boring, so boring, I had a more interesting job). The key must list them all or the task should give more guidance (e.g. 'use interesting').","level_problem":"","sense_problem":""},
